a52sxq 6.12 audio: 5.4 parity for the HAL's PCM ids and the Bluetooth back ends (2026-11-18)

Offline parity audit (drivers612/PARITY-2026-11-18.md, P0 items 1 and 2). Compiled only.

1. asoc/msm-dai-fe.c: FE DAI "MultiMedia11" (hw:24) is a PCM again. The Samsung HAL opens
   hw:24 as primary-playback; 5.4 drops .compress_new under CONFIG_SEC_SND_PRIMARY, the port
   had kept msm_fe_compress_dai_ops (compress node C0D24, "cannot open device 24").
2. asoc/lahaina.c: link hw:43 "Compress3" is MultiMedia10 on msm-pcm-dsp.1 (PCM) as on 5.4,
   not MultiMedia20 on msm-compress-dsp.
3. asoc/lahaina.c: the 5.4 Bluetooth back-end table (SLIMBUS_7_RX/TX, msm_wcn_init,
   msm_wcn_ops) is compiled again and selected by the sound node property qcom,wcn-btfm
   (empty or <1>); <2> selects Qualcomm's 3-link table (adds SLIMBUS_8_TX). qcom,wcn-bt stays
   ignored (see the comment in populate_snd_card_dailinks). Codec name stays
   "btfmslim_slave": that is what drivers612/conn/bt/btfmslim registers (built with
   -DCONFIG_BTFM_SLIM).

Apply in audio-kernel/ with: patch -p1 < this file (after a52-audit-2026-11-18.patch).

